title Why checkout timed out on Tuesday
sub example/charts @1a2b3c4
base app/

== timing Two workers, one row lock
axis: ms 0..400
api: API worker @checkout/api.py:40 # holds the order lock while it charges
  0 (idle) | 40 read cart | 70 *charge card | 250 +write paid | 300 (idle)
worker: Retry worker @jobs/retry.py:12
  0 (idle) | 90 read order | 120 !waits on lock | 280 write | 330 (idle)
!race: 120..250 worker blocked on the order row
*slow: 70..250 card provider call

== gantt Checkout request, critical path
axis: ms
budget: 600
auth: Auth check 0..40 @api/auth.py:8
cart: Load cart 60ms after auth
price: Price + tax 80ms after cart @pricing/tax.py:20
stock: Reserve stock 120ms after cart # warehouse API
!pay: Charge card 520ms after price @payments/charge.py:31 # provider p99
mail: Queue receipt 20ms after pay, stock

== causes Why the receipt email went missing
effect: no receipt # 3% of orders
-- deploy
-flag: mail flag off # checked: on in prod
?cfg: SMTP config drift
-- queue
+drop: hook raised before :240 @orders/order_service.py:236 # stops the chain
-full: queue full
-- data
?addr: bad email address
-- provider
-bounce: provider bounce # none in logs

== board Backfill, by shard
columns: queued | copying 3 | verifying | done
-- queued
s7: shard 7
s8: shard 8
-- copying
*s4: shard 4
  progress: 0.62
*s5: shard 5
  progress: 41%
!s6: shard 6 # lock wait on orders
  owner: backfill-2
-- verifying
s3: shard 3
-- done
+s1: shard 1
+s2: shard 2

== stock Email queue depth
unit: k
stock: email queue @mail/queue.py:10
meter: depth | 0 ok | 20 slow | 50 shedding | 80
9:00 2 | in 9k/min | out 8k/min
9:10 6
9:20 14 | in 14k/min # campaign starts
9:30 31 | out 6k/min # provider throttles
9:40 58
9:50 64 | in 4k/min
10:00 49 | out 12k/min # second provider on
10:10 27
10:20 9 | in 3k/min

== graph Where checkout requests go
view: sankey
web: Web
app: App
api: API
pay: Charge
fraud: Fraud check
paid: Paid
declined: Declined
blocked: Blocked
w1: web > pay => paid
  weight: 6200
w2: web > fraud =| blocked
  weight: 300
w3: app > pay => paid
  weight: 2600
!w4: app > pay > declined
  weight: 700
a1: api > pay => paid
  weight: 900
a2: api > fraud > pay => paid
  weight: 200

== graph Checkout, state as it changes
view: seq
browser: Browser
  state: cart
api: API [service]
  state: idle
pay: Payment provider
  state: ready
browser -> api: POST /checkout
  sets: api=*charging
api -> pay: charge
  sets: pay=*authorising
pay -> api: ok
  sets: pay=+captured, api=*writing
api -> browser: 200 paid
  sets: api=+done, browser=+receipt
checkout: browser > api > pay > api > browser | POST /checkout | The API holds the order while the provider authorises.
